    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_01ec7239a0dc79a569fe08366548c13477a25dba5bffbfe30f32f42af9ee3635",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The measure-theoretic toolkit forms a regularity ladder. Weak convergence and locally uniform convergence of characteristic functions identify limiting value measures; weighted integrability of the Fourier transform yields continuous densities and derivatives, while exponential transform decay yields real analyticity and arbitrarily strong exponential decay yields entire extension. Weak convergence alone does not grant any of the stronger spatial regularity.",
