    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_95f43c272eab19b163584493cd1a630bb6d8b8509144be10da3e7e39f857136f",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The area theorem turns preimages of values under f into a derivative-squared-weighted measure, and Fubini integrates that measure across a strip. When the weighted value measures have a jointly continuous density, this inverse-image density forces differentiability and a curvature relation for the Jensen function of f-x. Without absolute and joint continuity, the argument yields only semicontinuous bounds rather than the smooth curvature statement.",
