    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_56e9efa29e2b2928aad96c684d7f2d25a8551c3aa77ccdfe007a46c483e082c1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The density theory is modular: head-tail concentration gives rapid spatial decay, divergent total phase radii give geometric reach and positivity, inverse-radius growth determines how much Fourier decay is available for analytic continuation, parameter-uniform bounds control families and boundary escape, and exponentiation transports the additive log-value laws to multiplicative value laws only after summing all logarithmic sheets with the correct Jacobian. These conclusions depend on separate resources and do not imply one another.",
